mode: "100644"
text: "# Strategic Commenting\n\nCommenting on **other people's** posts — the under-used growth play where a good comment borrows\nsomeone else's (highly relevant) audience. ~41% of brands now leave proactive comments on others'\nposts to boost visibility, and when a comment **sparks a reply, engagement jumps ~1.6×**. On LinkedIn\nit's a *primary* growth channel; it works on IG/TikTok/X too.\n\n> Re-verify specifics quarterly; the principle (value-adding comments borrow audiences) is durable.\n\n## Why it grows you\n\n- **Borrowed audience.** A genuinely valuable comment on a bigger account's post is seen by *their*\n  audience — exactly the people you want — and drives curious profile visits back to you.\n- **Comments get their own reach.** On several platforms comments now earn their own impressions, so a\n  sharp comment is a tiny piece of content in its own right.\n- **It compounds your authority.** Consistently smart comments in your lane mark you as a knowledgeable\n  voice in the niche (reinforces the topic authority the growth skills rely on → `linkedin-growth`,\n  `instagram-growth`, `tiktok-growth`).\n\n## The value rubric (what to actually write)\n\nA strategic comment must **add value** — it earns attention, it doesn't beg for it. Good comments:\n\n- **Add an insight** the post didn't cover (\"This matches what we saw — the nuance is X…\").\n- **Respectfully disagree and explain** (\"I'd push back on point 2, because…\") — the highest-engagement\n  type, done in good faith.\n- **Build on it** with a concrete example, a number, or a next step.\n- **Ask a genuinely good question** that moves the discussion forward.\n- Are **substantive** — aim for real sentences (15+ words), in your brand voice.\n\n**Never:**\n- \"Great post! 🙌\" / \"So true!\" / \"Thanks for sharing\" — worthless, and increasingly *blocked and\n  reported* as spam.\n- **Veiled self-promo** (\"Love this — we actually built a tool for this, check my bio\") — it reads as\n  hijacking and burns goodwill.\n- **AI-obvious / automated** comments — detected, ignored, and penalized (see the no-automation rule in\n  `dms-hard-cases-and-safety.md`).\n\n## Where to spend the time (the right rooms)\n\n- **In your lane** — comment on topics you're credible on, so the people who discover you are the right\n  ones.\n- **On ICP + niche thought leaders** — the accounts whose audience *is* your audience. A viral comment\n  in front of the wrong crowd builds nothing (see \"the right people, not vanity\" in\n  `dms-hard-cases-and-safety.md`).\n- **On posts with momentum, early** — commenting thoughtfully while a post is climbing gets your comment\n  (and you) more eyes.\n\n## Honest framing\n\nThis is **genuine participation done consistently**, not a hack. It works because the comments are\nactually good and actually yours. The agent **drafts** strong, on-voice comments for the human to post\nin real conversations — it does **not** spray automated comments across hundreds of accounts (that's\nspam, and it backfires).\n"
